task: intent-active-learning
agent: fable-persist
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/intent-active-learning
worktree: ../okay-wt-al

why: "labels are the bottleneck everywhere above, so choose the next
  ones to label by uncertainty rather than by order" — a claim the
  fixture can test without a single new label, because its labels
  are all known: simulate the labelling and count what a chosen label
  is worth against one taken in order or at random.

what: TestActiveLearning (Live for the one embedding, offline after):
  the pool is the training half, the seed eight rows (two per
  class), each round adds four — by the probe's smallest margin over
  the unlabelled pool, by the fixture's order, or at random (five
  seeds, the mean); probe and centroid refitted each round and scored
  on the held-out half; both mirror splits; the area between the
  curves and the labels each strategy needs to reach 80%. Boards: this
  entry, and intent-ensemble-weights kept gated with its reason (the
  corpus did not grow honestly — intent-distil-dose/-static/-diversity).
